SECTION 1 — APPLICATION OVERVIEW
======================================================

Application Purpose
A multi-market autonomous algorithmic trading platform combining a high-performance Go execution engine (v6.0), a Python AI strategy service, and a Next.js dashboard. It supports paper trading (mock), live trading (Binance futures, Angel One equities, Delta Exchange options), and a multi-agent AI research tournament for strategy promotion. Phase 11–14 additions include a full institutional infrastructure layer: OMS v3, event-sourced ledger, kill switch, reconciliation service, ML classifier, Redis performance cache, TimescaleDB schema, and 9 new microstructure alpha strategies.

Main Features
Real-time BTC perpetual futures paper and live trading via Coinbase WebSocket (primary), Binance REST, Delta Exchange
100+ registered price-based strategies plus 9 new Phase-11 microstructure alpha strategies
Multi-model AI consensus engine (GPT-4o, GPT-4o-mini, Gemini Flash 2.0, Groq Llama-3-70b) with 6-provider fallback chain
ML classifier (engine/internal/ml/) as low-latency replacement path for LLM council
CVD Divergence, Funding Rate Edge, Liquidity Sweep Reversal, Fair Value Gap, Market Structure Shift, Order Block, Volume Profile VPOC, Liquidation Cascade, Delta Divergence (all Phase 11 — NEW)
Research tournament: strategies earn promotion by hitting statistical thresholds (unchanged, best-in-class)
Kill switch with 8 trigger types and 4 action types (Phase 12 — NEW)
Event-sourced order ledger with SHA-256 hashed payloads (Phase 12 — NEW)
OMS v3 with 9-state aggregate state machine (Phase 14 — NEW)
Reconciliation service: OMS vs exchange state comparison (Phase 14 — NEW)
Risk gate pipeline: composable pre-trade checks (Phase 13 — NEW)
Redis performance cache layer: AI decisions, strategy rankings, live positions (Phase 14 — NEW)
TimescaleDB Phase 14 schema: event store, tick data, order/fill/position projections (Phase 14 — NEW)
Options chain viewer (Delta Exchange — BTC)
NIFTY 50 options and equities (Angel One / NSE)
MCX commodities (crude oil, gold — data feed)
Full analytics: Sharpe, Sortino, Calmar, Monte Carlo, equity curves
Dual persistence: MongoDB Atlas + SQLite + PostgreSQL/TimescaleDB + Redis

