SECTION 2 — TRADING SYSTEM AUDIT
======================================================

How Signals Are Generated
Signals are generated in three ways:

1. Go Engine — Strategy Registry (engine/internal/strategy/)
Each of the 100+ registered strategies implements the Strategy interface:
  OnTick(tick Tick) []Signal     — evaluated on every raw WebSocket trade tick
  OnCandle(candle Tick) []Signal — evaluated when a new OHLCV candle closes
Each Signal carries: Symbol, Action (BUY/SELL/HOLD), Confidence (0–1), TargetSize, StopLossPct, TakeProfitPct, AIDecisionID, AIReasoning.

2. Go Engine — Alpha Engine (engine/internal/alpha/)  ← NEW Phase 11
Nine new microstructure modules each expose an Evaluate(symbol, prices) Signal method
using the alpha.Signal type (alpha/types.go). Signals carry Source, QualityScore, and
custom SL/TP geometry suited to each edge type (e.g. CVD: SL 0.30%, TP 0.75%).

3. Client-Side Mock Engine (client/src/lib/mockTradingEngine.ts)
Signals arrive via API from the research tournament carrying signal_score, confidence_score,
quality_score, mtf_score, and regime classification.

How Trades Are Created

Signal produced by strategy or alpha module
  → Signal aggregation: cooldown filter (15-min), dedup, regime gate
  → AI council vote (Bull/Bear/Macro/Risk) OR ML classifier decision
  → If confidence < 0.82 → park in pendingSignals (manual review, not executed)
  → Pre-trade risk gate: context → kill switch → engine → inputs → risk decision
  → Risk Engine Validate() — 5 gate checks
  → Execution Router: MARKET / POST_ONLY / IOC by category + regime
  → PaperOMS.Open() OR BinanceLive.PlaceOrder()
  → Position created: entryPrice, SL, TP, liquidationPrice, maxHold
  → Entry fee deducted (0.05% taker), entry slippage applied (5 bps adverse)
  → Ledger event: PositionOpenedEvent appended (SHA-256 hashed)
  → Event bus: EventPositionOpened published to subscribers

How Positions Are Managed
The PaperOMS (engine/internal/execution/paper_oms.go) maintains a []PaperPosition slice
(deterministic insertion-order iteration, sync.Mutex held for all operations). On each tick:

Each open position is evaluated: check SL hit, TP hit, max hold (45 min), margin breach
Breakeven move triggered at 40% progress to TP (CurrentSL moved to entryPrice)
Trailing stop triggered at 65% progress to TP (gives back 35% of move from peak)
If margin < 0.5% maintenance threshold → LIQUIDATION_RISK close

How Exits Are Handled
Eight exit types are defined (ExitReasonProfitLock added in Phase 12):

Exit Reason         Trigger Condition
TP                  Price crosses take-profit price
SL                  Price crosses stop-loss (or trailing stop)
TIME                Position age > 45 minutes
TRAIL               Trailing stop triggered after 65% progress to TP
BREAKEVEN           SL moved to breakeven after 40% progress to TP
LIQUIDATION_RISK    Margin < 0.5% maintenance threshold
MANUAL              User closes via API
PROFIT_LOCK         Reserved for profit-lock mechanism (Phase 12)

On exit: exit price calculated with 5 bps adverse slippage, exit fee (0.05%) deducted,
PnL recorded, position removed from openPositions slice, CloseEvent emitted.

How TP/SL Works
LONG:   SL = entryPrice × (1 - slPct),   TP = entryPrice × (1 + tpPct)
SHORT:  SL = entryPrice × (1 + slPct),   TP = entryPrice × (1 - tpPct)
Min R:R: 1.5 (mock engine), 2.0 (AI constitution), 2.40 (engine target)
AI agents enforce tight geometry: SL 0.12–0.20%, TP 0.20–0.32%
CVD/Alpha strategies use wider geometry: SL 0.30%, TP 0.75%

How Fees Are Calculated
Model: Binance/Delta taker fee = 0.05% per leg
Round-trip: 0.10% total (open + close)
Applied in Paper OMS: fee deducted from virtual cash on both open and close
Applied in mock engine: same fee model (0.05% taker) + 5 bps slippage per side
Fee drag monitoring: fee_pct_of_gross tracked per strategy — DISABLE verdict if fee/gross > 100%
Note: mockTradingEngine.ts comment references "Delta India futures rate" — minor labelling difference, same 0.05% value

How Funding Is Calculated
PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED — alpha/funding/ implements a funding rate collector (funding_collector.go
polls Binance /fapi/v1/fundingRate) and a funding strategy (short when rate > 0.1%, long when < -0.05%).
However, funding cost is NOT yet subtracted from Paper OMS PnL on open positions.
This means reported expectancy is inflated for long-duration longs by approximately 0.03–0.05%/day.
This is a known gap and the highest-priority PnL correction item.

How PnL Is Calculated
Unrealized PnL (LONG):  (currentPrice - entryPrice) / entryPrice × notional × leverage - fees
Unrealized PnL (SHORT): (entryPrice - currentPrice) / entryPrice × notional × leverage - fees
Realized PnL:           Calculated on close with slippage-adjusted exit price and exit fee
Account Equity:         startingBalance + sum(realizedPnL) + sum(unrealizedPnL)
Expectancy:             (winRate × avgWin) - ((1 - winRate) × avgLoss)

