Exposure Controls
maxOpenTrades: 5 total
maxLongPositions: 3
maxShortPositions: 3
Checked in evaluateMockTradeOpenRisk() — lines 617–622 (mockTradingEngine.ts)

Cooldown Controls
15-minute lockout per strategy ID
Enforced by tracking last-entry timestamp per strategy
Resets 15 minutes from last filled trade (not from last signal)

Risk Limits
Daily loss: 3% of starting equity
Weekly loss: 6% of starting equity
Max drawdown: 10%
Minimum R:R: 1.5
Minimum signal score: 50 (hardcoded in DEFAULT_MOCK_TRADING_CONFIG)

Why Mock Trading Most Commonly Fails to Generate Trades
In order of likelihood for a fresh deployment:
1. NO_APPROVED_STRATEGY — Zero promoted strategies at cold start. System idles until
   12 trades per strategy accumulate and the daily cron awards PROMOTE verdict.
2. LOW_SIGNAL_SCORE — quality_score and mtf_score may not be populated by all signal
   sources. Without them, threshold bonus is the only additive component and scores stay < 50.
3. REGIME — BTC spends ~40% of time ranging. NO_TRADE classification blocks all signals.
4. Cold-start candle gap — Ichimoku (52 bars), Pivot (60 bars), MTF RSI (52+ bars) produce
   no signals for up to 60 minutes after engine restart.
5. EXPOSURE_LIMIT — If account already has 5 open positions from prior session, new signals
   are blocked until positions close.
6. DAILY_LOSS_LIMIT — After a 3% daily loss, all new trades are blocked until midnight.
7. AI Council veto — Risk Arbitrator blocks trades when ADX < 15 or price > 0.4% from VWAP.
   In ranging markets this alone can suppress 80%+ of signals.

