SECTION 18 — FINAL VERDICT (PHASE 14)
======================================================

1. What is the biggest weakness?
Security remains completely unaddressed through Phases 11–14. Live exchange API credentials
(GROQ, Delta) sit in the .env file. The database password is password123. Every Go engine
endpoint — including /api/delta-live/enable, /api/admin/killswitch, and /paper/open — has zero
authentication. A Delta Exchange account with live options trading capability (live_bridge.go)
has its HMAC credentials accessible to anyone who can read the .env file or git history.
This is no longer theoretical: Phases 11–14 added significant institutional capability while
leaving the door to the account unlocked. Security must be addressed before any of the new
alpha strategies or live trading features are enabled.

2. What is the biggest strength?
The combination of the research tournament (unchanged, best-in-class) and the Phase 11
microstructure alpha engine. Eight of the highest-edge BTC perpetual signals — CVD divergence,
funding rate mean-reversion, liquidity sweep reversal, volume profile VPOC, fair value gaps,
liquidation cascade reversals, market structure shift, and order block detection — are now
code-complete. These are the signals that professional BTC desks trade. The platform is the
only retail system in the market that combines a statistically rigorous research promotion system
with this class of institutional alpha signals. That combination is genuinely differentiated.

3. What is the biggest architectural risk?
The dual OMS. The legacy paper_oms.go is confirmed active. OMS v3 (omsv3/aggregate.go) is
implemented but its relationship to the live execution path is unverified. Both tracking position
state independently will eventually produce a reconciliation failure. The reconciliation service
(reconciliation/service.go) will detect this — but if OMS v3 is receiving events that paper_oms
is not (or vice versa), the correction actions in sync.go may not be able to resolve it. The
priority is: pick one OMS, confirm it as primary, deprecate the other, and verify with tests.

4. Why might mock trading not generate trades?
Same causes as Phase 1, ranked by likelihood:
1. NO_APPROVED_STRATEGY — Zero strategies promoted at cold start. System idles until
   12 trades per strategy accumulate and the daily cron awards PROMOTE.
2. Alpha strategies blocked — CVD, Funding, FVG etc. are NOT wired to registry. The 9
   highest-edge strategies produce no signals in the mock engine.
3. REGIME — BTC ranging ~40% of time. NO_TRADE classification suppresses all signals.
